The content candidate is the universal inequality from the explicit constructed
eight-term nonnegative decomposition, not a normalization helper or a new
generic positivity theorem. The raw coefficients are used only in rhs and its
proofs; there is no standalone finite validity assertion.
Numerical premises for the same real length-28 domain and the upper threshold
1/25 are fulfilled in certificate_identity and certificate_nonnegative.
certificate_identity expands the exact real polynomial. In certificate_nonnegative,
hp checks P's LDL identity and 27 pivot signs; hb checks the 52 interior B LDL
identities and 156 pivot signs, plus the four rank-one endpoint signs; hd checks
four D LDL identities and 12 pivot signs; hs and hm check three C LDL identities
and six pivot signs. hh, hw and hg check the 784 H, 28 w and two gamma signs
at the summands where they are used. All 60 LDL identities and 201 pivot signs
are local premises of real quadratic or trace inequalities. The gap, pencil
and L4 hypotheses belong to that same spectrum. These two universal helpers
are used directly by purity_bound; neither helper is an escape witness alone.
